# LINE ENDINGS: LF in the repo AND on disk. `eol=lf` rather than a bare
# `text=auto`, because the point is the WORKING TREE - on Windows core.autocrlf
# would otherwise write CRLF out at checkout, and that is what breaks.
#
# This is not cosmetic. An addon travels as a .mastlib ZIP, and MAST reads a
# zipped entry as BYTES (`f.read().decode()`, mast.py:948) where it reads the
# same file from a FOLDER in Python text mode (mast.py:966), which silently
# translates CRLF away. So one committed .mast parses two different ways
# depending on where it was read from - and the zipped way does not parse at
# all: on CRLF the label header rule stops matching, `== label ==` becomes an
# unrecognized line, and a story that compiles to no labels still reports PASS.
#
# `sbs lib` builds mastlibs from the working tree, so a Windows clone without
# this line packages broken addons. The release workflow runs on ubuntu-latest
# and was never exposed, which is why nothing shipped broken and nobody noticed.
#
# Renormalizing an EXISTING clone needs a delete-and-restore of the tracked
# files: `git checkout-index -a -f` does nothing, because the index caches the
# checkout's stat - which is also why `git status` calls a CRLF tree clean.
# `git ls-files --eol` is the honest check (`i/lf w/crlf` = mangled).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The only binaries in the tree. Declared rather than left to auto-detection.
*.png binary

*.mast linguist-language=Python
*.amd linguist-language=markdown

# The GitHub ARCHIVE (what `sbs.pyz fetch` downloads) leaves these out; a clone and the
# release workflow's `actions/checkout` still get everything, so the media pack is built
# from the real art as before. `export-ignore` only governs `git archive`.
#
# media/ travels as its own release asset instead - unpacked ONCE into `__lib__/media`
# and read from there, rather than copied into every mission that uses it. story.json
# declares it under `shared_media`, which resolves mission-local first, so a clone keeps
# editing art in place.
media/          export-ignore
mkdocs/         export-ignore
.github/        export-ignore

# The 34 ADDON folders travel as .mastlib release assets, the same way media/ does.
# A fetched copy therefore has no addon source and loads them from `__lib__` (they are
# declared in story.json); a CLONE still has every folder and MAST prefers the source,
# so editing an addon in place keeps working. Keep this list in step with
# __lib__.json - it is the single source of truth for what gets packaged.
